<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Surb Karapet Monastery</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Glak Monastery, Monastery of Saint John the Precursor</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Surb Karapet, the Monastery of the Holy Forerunner, stood near Muş in the historic Armenian district of Taron. Tradition holds that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gregory-the-illuminator">Gregory the Illuminator</a> founded it in the 4th century to house relics of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-the-baptist">John the Baptist</a>, and it became one of the most revered pilgrimage sites of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>. It was abandoned and destroyed after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">genocide</a> of 1915.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/surb-karapet-monastery.jpg" alt="Surb Karapet Monastery" width="320" height="258" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vartan A. Hampikian · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Surb_Karapet_Monastery_Hampikian_LoC.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
